# config/defconfigs/vf2.config — StarFive VisionFive 2 (JH7110) — Edge profile
#
# Target: VisionFive 2 SBC, 8 GiB LPDDR4, JH7110 SoC (4-core rv64gc @ 1.5 GHz,
#         no RVV hardware).  Primary bring-up target for July 2026 hardware.
#
# Memory budget (rough):
#   Static tables (RFC-0023 edge): ~3-4 MiB
#   Kernel heap (KERNEL_HEAP_SIZE = 32768 KiB): 32 MiB
#   Lazy user stacks (MAX_TASKS=64 × 16 KiB demand-paged): ~1 MiB physical
#   Total worst-case: ~36-37 MiB  (well within 8 GiB VF2 RAM)
#
# Notable vs. edge defaults:
#   BOARD=VF2 (MACB Ethernet enabled, VirtIO disabled, JH7110 UART/CSI/I2C).
#   RISCV64_LEVEL=rv64gc, RV_V=n (board defaults) — JH7110 has no Vector extension.
#   TIMER_FREQ=4000000  — JH7110 CLINT runs at 4 MHz (matches the platform.rs
#     source-of-truth value tagged "← critical difference" in
#     crates/drivers/base/src/platform.rs).  Earlier drafts of RFC-0026 inferred
#     16 MHz incorrectly; the real reference-manual value is 4 MHz.  Kept at
#     the Kconfig default — no override needed.
#   SCHED_HZ=250 (PROFILE_EDGE && BOARD_VF2 default, JH7110 1.5 GHz can handle it).
#   WCET_BOUND_TIMER_ISR_US=10 (real hardware, not QEMU TCG).
#   DRV_MACB_ETHERNET=y (auto from BOARD_VF2 default).
#   DRV_VIRTIO_BLK_NET=n (auto from !BOARD_QEMU).
#   DRV_USB_MSC_GADGET=y, DRV_USB_DFU_RECOVERY=y (BOARD_VF2 defaults).
#
# Used for: VF2 hardware bring-up.
#
# Regenerate with:  make defconfig-vf2 && make savedefconfig
# CONFIG_DOMAIN_ROBOT=y (wave 11, DOMAIN): this image is the robot worked
# example, and the gate's robot rows build from it. The domain is what links
# the robot crates (kernel feature `domain-robot`); `make config` from
# scratch defaults to DOMAIN_GENERIC.
CONFIG_DOMAIN_ROBOT=y

CONFIG_BOARD_VF2=y

# Ring-3 driver proxy spin before blocking (config/Kconfig.drivers PROXY_SPIN_US).
# 20 us is the QEMU-measured value; the symbol's help says how to measure
# it on this board.
CONFIG_PROXY_SPIN_US=20
